{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful","id":183320,"title":"Angels - How powerful?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-28T16:29:59-07:00","id":183320,"title":"Angels - How powerful?","content":"I have a problem understanding the angels power level.<br /> <br /> Let me start by saying that I've never been much impressed by numina. While they in theory could have some uses, they are quite expensive for what they do, and are in no way sustainable with the limited essence pools spirits have. If it's one thing that makes spirits powerful is their huge dice pools, as their rank go up, and correlated health levels.<br /> <br /> Angels are spirits. As such, their dicepool is powerful, but their powers are not. They don't have much essence, and they can outdice their opponents pretty well, but that's about this. Rank 2 angels are no big deal. Rank 4+ angels, with their dicepools, can outdice any demon pc.<br /> <br /> But, then come the embeds. In the demons description, they had instinctive knowledge of all the embeds related to their incarnation. Then they lost it when they fell. Embeds are pretty powerful, and arguably the major benefit when you go loud is your ability to use all of your incarnation embeds (and exploits, of course).<br /> <br /> But, if even the lowest GM angels could use all the embeds, they would be massively powerful. They could outdice any demon, and would have limitless embeds to use (exploits printed and unprinted). Not only that, but they would be pretty unmanageble. What storyteller could use adroitly a list of 50+ embeds? They would also have to practically never use essence, give how much versatile and powerful their infinite embeds are than numina.<br /> <br /> How do you deal with angels? How powerful do you make them? Do you handave the embeds, saying that their huge dicepools are an abstraction for their embeds? Do you run their with all incarnation embeds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":".  GMC is not Exalted, Essence is not Rank! 06-29-2014, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T20:41:14-07:00","id":183455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful#post183320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What storyteller could use adroitly a list of 50+ embeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one, so don't bother. Angels have command line access to reality.<br /> <br /> If the demons are fleeing an angel and get into their car to get away. The angel approaches a car (<i>any</i> car) in the parking lot, enters it, turns it on. No roll necessary.<br /> <br /> Every light turns red. No roll necessary.<br /> <br /> Sleeper agents in the area activate and start trying to ram the characters' car. No roll necessary for the angel, contested drive rolls verses the sleepers.<br /> <br /> Let the players do the work of hashing out an escape plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful#post183320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do you deal with angels? How powerful do you make them? Do you handave the exploits, saying that their huge dicepools are an abstraction for their embeds? Do you run their with all incarnation embeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Use them sparingly, and make the players cautious in dealing with them.<br /> 2. As powerful as they need to to accomplish whatever task the G-M has given them. The G-M has finite resources it can devote to a project; not every angel has Rank 10.<br /> 3. Angels don't use embed or exploits, those are work-arounds that demons use to emulate the abilities they used to have. But yes, hand-waving a large dice pool is a smart way to maintain pacing.<br /> 4. Yes. Plus a few other tricks. Angels aren't prevented from cross-specializing if it suits the G-Ms purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 06-29-2014, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T21:57:48-07:00","id":183512,"title":"","content":"Please top using Essence when you mean Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T22:37:52-07:00","id":183524,"title":"","content":"And Numina when you mean Influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T22:54:56-07:00","id":183544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183512#post183512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please top using Essence when you mean Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my exalted is showing! I did that without thinking, there, fixed! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:15:57-07:00","id":183571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183455#post183455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one, so don't bother. Angels have command line access to reality.<br /> <br /> If the demons are fleeing an angel and get into their car to get away. The angel approaches a car (<i>any</i> car) in the parking lot, enters it, turns it on. No roll necessary.<br /> <br /> Every light turns red. No roll necessary.<br /> <br /> Sleepers in the area activate and start trying to ram the characters' car. No roll necessary for the angel, contested drive rolls verses the sleepers.<br /> <br /> Let the players do the work of hashing out an escape plan.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd rather have some guidelines in a way to have them powerful, but fair. With as little handwave as possible. I am thinking something like: while an Angel has access to every embed, their lack of creativity and static reasoning make them able to use, say, one embed per rank? They can be repourposed later. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Use them sparingly, and make the players cautious in dealing with them.<br /> 2. As powerful as they need to to accomplish whatever task the G-M has given them. The G-M has finite resources it can devote to a project; not every angel has essence 10.<br /> 3. Angels don't use embed or exploits, those are work-arounds that demons use to emulate the abilities they used to have. But yes, hand-waving a large dice pool is a smart way to maintain pacing.<br /> 4. Yes. Plus a few other tricks. Angels aren't prevented from cross-specializing if it suits the G-Ms purpose. </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> 1. Of course angels should not be used all the time, but they are the arm of the G-M, and it's everywhere. Players should get themselves in trouble with the G-M all the time, and mortals and stigmatics don't pass the muster as sufficient opposition for demons. <br /> 2. Yes, but how good the the G-M foresight? It can't be perfect, since angels fail all the time and there are demons at large. So, they should have stats and still be able to fall short of their objectives. <br /> 3. The gist I got from Embeds is that they are cheats the G-M has placed for their angels that the demons can still access. So, they are basically the same for both creatures. Exploits, though, are a new thing.<br /> 4. I was thiking more of the dichotomy of the Angels as spirits vs. Angels as Going Loud Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:19:16-07:00","id":183572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183524#post183524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Numina when you mean Influences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What? Well, influence is all nice and good, but most example angels have got numina, while just some have got influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:27:21-07:00","id":183574,"title":"","content":"All spirits, be they Ghosts, Angels, or Spirits have an Influence, and also have Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:28:48-07:00","id":183575,"title":"","content":"All of them have Influences and all of them have Numina. They're two different Traits that all Ephemeral Beings have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:31:14-07:00","id":183576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183572#post183572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What? Well, influence is all nice and good, but most example angels have got numina, while just some have got influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, every angel has both. As does every ghost and every spirit. You might want to review the ephemeral entities rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:22:37-07:00","id":183604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183572#post183572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Well, influence is all nice and good, but most example angels have got numina, while just some have got influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the parts the others have corrected you on, Numina are not expensive and they can be used to replicate the effects of essentially any published supernatural power on the books to some degree, while Influences have a scaling cost and require Rank 3 at minimum to enable most Influences to be overtly useful, so your complaints about Numina ring false unless you are in fact experiencing the aforementioned nomenclatural difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T07:15:52-07:00","id":183771,"title":"","content":"You do not need to hand wave anything. Demons try to escape in a car, the hunter angel has Finesse + Rank. Rank is used in place of any skill, save for where Attribute + Attribute is made instead (such as with perception). It specifically says that any task an angel needs to accomplish it can use Rank on, because that is part of its mission. If it tries to perform a task outside its mission, it cannot. (But angels are always on mission, if they're not, there is going to be a really big bang in a moment! and the demon's will have a new friend! ...or enemy?)<br /> <br /> Angels also have influences. All Ephemeral Entities have dots equal to their rank in Influences. An Angel's influences are things related to either (or both) it's nature or it's mission. Depending on how many dots it has in these influences, it is able to do more with them.<br /> <br /> In the above example, the demons are attempting to get away in a car. The angel is in pursuit. Slowing down the demon's by changing the traffic signs is within the scope of it's mission (It's a destroyer angel sent to chase and kill demons who will, of course, attempt escape). So, it rolls Finesse + Rank and you, as the storyteller simply decide whether success means all lights along the road go red, or a number of lights equal to rank or successes. Activating the sleepers in a nearby car? Power + Rank, each success awakens a mortal as a sleeper agent. (Not all mortals are sleeper agents, but one-shot NPC fodder don't need to be explained, Angels are adept at using whatever resources they happen to have in their local environment). Starting the car? Finesse + Rank, success turns the vehicle on. Finesse+Rank drives it.<br /> <br /> These are all solid rolls you as the story teller make and -could- fail on, either to represent an angel's momentary hesitation or confusion, or encountering a situation it does not know how to easily resolve quickly. This general performance in light of its mission affords angels some of the greatest power, and indeed gives them whatever tools they happen to need to perform their mission. Embeds and Exploits represent individual hacks the Demons have created in an effort to replicate this ability along with the more specific abilities of Numina.<br /> <br /> Or so is my understanding of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:12:28-07:00","id":183801,"title":"","content":"I gather that I have forgotten how influence works (and I remember now why I've forgotten them, too). The thing is, given the space constraints for it (the rules cover what, two pages?), it can be a little too vague, IMO. It changes from 'minor' changes to 'dramatic' ones from influence 2 to 3 without any example of what is the scope of each. This is something I feel that could use a little more development to be actually usable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183604#post183604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the parts the others have corrected you on, Numina are not expensive and they can be used to replicate the effects of essentially any published supernatural power on the books to some degree, while Influences have a scaling cost and require Rank 3 at minimum to enable most Influences to be overtly useful, so your complaints about Numina ring false unless you are in fact experiencing the aforementioned nomenclatural difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, give me a way to simulate cheaply Just Bruised as a numina effect, with the same scope (armor only goes so far). Cool heads prevail is a simple embed that costs nothing and plays with the emotions of multiple people, but the only way I figure to simulate it is with influence 5, and that costs 5 essence to use. Alibi, In my Pocket, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:18:39-07:00","id":183812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183801#post183801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gather that I have forgotten how influence works (and I remember now why I've forgotten them, too). The thing is, given the space constraints for it (the rules cover what, two pages?), it can be a little too vague, IMO. It changes from 'minor' changes to 'dramatic' ones from influence 2 to 3 without any example of what is the scope of each. This is something I feel that could use a little more development to be actually usable. Ok, give me a way to simulate cheaply Just Bruised as a numina effect, with the same scope (armor only goes so far). Cool heads prevail is a simple embed that costs nothing and plays with the emotions of multiple people, but the only way I figure to simulate it is with influence 5, and that costs 5 essence to use. Alibi, In my Pocket, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just make a Numen that has that effect. Boom, done. Numen can do what ever the story needs them to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:42:44-07:00","id":183840,"title":"","content":"Just Bruised: Influence effect 1: Strengthen. Add successes to the Defense of your influence. Thus removing incoming attack dice. If that's not what you like, if you can add to the defense of a loved one by strengthening them, then you can take away damage that would be dealt to them! So, remove successes damage from the target of the influence instead. Numina is not exhaustive list, if these two effects are not suitable for you, then simply make it a 1 Essence Numina that reduces all incoming damage on a target to 1. (Do remember that Angels are always storyteller characters so powers like Just Bruised make them very difficult to kill when they are already statistically superior. There is a mechanical aspect, unless you're just wanting to make a monster that your players cannot have a hope of defeating.)<br /> <br /> Cool Heads Prevail: Influence effect 3: Control. If the influence is emotion, you turn it off in everyone within the area of your influence. Note: Mass Create means you can create multiple instances of a condition. There is nothing to prevent you using 3 dot Control to effect more than one person in a scene. Again, create a Numen that replicates the effect otherwise.<br /> <br /> Alibi is replicated by the Manfestation: Image. If you are upset about RAW, modify to cost the same to project an image of the angel's form.<br /> <br /> In My Pocket: Angels are always prepared for their mission. They have what they need. When in doubt? Attribute + Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 06-29-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T10:48:50-07:00","id":183880,"title":"","content":"DesolateDolly, I wish I could give out cookies over the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T14:44:46-07:00","id":184100,"title":"","content":"Here's a related question: When Angels use Embeds as Numina, do you make them spend a single Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T16:58:49-07:00","id":184208,"title":"","content":"While it largely depends on the Embeds (not all Embeds are created equal - some are a little more bang for your buck, like Merciless Gunman or Just Bruised) I find it is easier to represent their effect with an Attribute + Rank roll, Influence effect or Manifestation effect.<br /> <br /> Also, C is for cookies and that is good enough for me! *Cavernous Maw*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 06-30-2014, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:46:59-07:00","id":190880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183840#post183840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just Bruised: Influence effect 1: Strengthen. Add successes to the Defense of your influence. Thus removing incoming attack dice. If that's not what you like, if you can add to the defense of a loved one by strengthening them, then you can take away damage that would be dealt to them! So, remove successes damage from the target of the influence instead. Numina is not exhaustive list, if these two effects are not suitable for you, then simply make it a 1 Essence Numina that reduces all incoming damage on a target to 1. (Do remember that Angels are always storyteller characters so powers like Just Bruised make them very difficult to kill when they are already statistically superior. There is a mechanical aspect, unless you're just wanting to make a monster that your players cannot have a hope of defeating.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite a fit. Just Bruised is reflexive, and can reduce a boundless amount a damage to one. You are describing a few points of armor. The scope is completely different. And of couse, I could handwave a numina. But then, why would this numina be so much more powerful that all the rest? No offense, but that's a rule zero fallacy if I've ever seen one.<br /> <br /> Of course, I agree that this embed can be troublesome for NPCs (of couse, demon npcs do exist). Just Bruised has a 'diminising effort' aspect that can make it somewhat workable, I would not recommend that with an angel's potential dicepool. But that's not the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool Heads Prevail: Influence effect 3: Control. If the influence is emotion, you turn it off in everyone within the area of your influence. Note: Mass Create means you can create multiple instances of a condition. There is nothing to prevent you using 3 dot Control to effect more than one person in a scene. Again, create a Numen that replicates the effect otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Not so, I'm quoting the book, influence 3: 'An animal's action, one plants's growth , or one object's functioning'. One individual until influence 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alibi is replicated by the Manfestation: Image. If you are upset about RAW, modify to cost the same to project an image of the angel's form. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In My Pocket: Angels are always prepared for their mission. They have what they need. When in doubt? Attribute + Rank. </div> </div> </div>So, no surprises for angels, right? That's ironic in a game of demons. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":".  would *not* recommend 07-08-2014, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T16:59:23-07:00","id":190900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=190880#post190880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense, but that's a rule zero fallacy if I've ever seen one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be clearer that you don't have a fucking clue what the Rule Zero Fallacy is, but not without getting into the realm of egregious hyperbole.<br /> <br /> Numina are the catch-all category for supernatural powers an ephemeral being uses that don't stem from Influences or possibly its shape. The ones we get as examples have to pull their weight for nearly every level of ephemeral being, but &quot;you can convert other supernatural powers into Numina to save us all some pagespace&quot; has been an explicit facet of the things for forever.<br /> <br /> None of this whinging about how an Embed whose category represents the affinities of <i>guardian angels</i> oughtn't scan fairly to a similar angel-Numen that allows one to drastically reduce physical damage done to themselves or a target in their presence is necessary or helpful to anybody, least of all yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:50:28-07:00","id":191003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=190900#post190900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Numina are the catch-all category for supernatural powers an ephemeral being uses that don't stem from Influences or possibly its shape. The ones we get as examples have to pull their weight for nearly every level of ephemeral being, but &quot;you can convert other supernatural powers into Numina to save us all some pagespace&quot; has been an explicit facet of the things for forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, until Hunter introduced Dread Powers but that's just splitting hairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T19:59:34-07:00","id":191045,"title":"","content":"Satchel did say ephemeral beings. Material beings use Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T22:33:36-07:00","id":191127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191045#post191045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel did say ephemeral beings. Material beings use Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've defined Dread Powers as more of a Hunter centric terminology of the powers of a monster, ephemeral or not.<br /> <br /> But then again, Hunter does play fast and loose with most rules and I think the GMC put into terms which accurately reflects your statement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T23:47:39-07:00","id":191151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div 