ake:<br /> <br /> <i>None of that has jack shit to do with my point of &quot;Numina have been explicitly able to draw from conversions of other published supernatural powers literally ever since the first corebook that included both Numina and non-Numen supernatural powers.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Focus on the fact that the car is going seventy miles per hour and moving directly toward you; its license plate is of secondary importance at best.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Also the Strix aren't ephemeral.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T00:08:40-07:00","id":191159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191151#post191151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Counterpoint: the Strix use Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not actually ephemeral beings and don't use their rules. <br /> <br /> But yeah, it's not a terribly important point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T03:00:46-07:00","id":191274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191159#post191159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, it's not a terribly important point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, hence the comment about splitting hairs.<br /> <br /> edit: Did Satchel get banned for this topic? As harsh as his tone sometimes is, I don't think it warrants a kick but what do I know. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-08-2014, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:27:23-07:00","id":191365,"title":"","content":"Give our Satchel back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T08:09:27-07:00","id":191400,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey guys, just a friendly reminder that it is against the rules to discuss moderator action publicly. If you have questions or concerns, please use the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\">contact us</a> link.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T10:28:50-07:00","id":191509,"title":"","content":"Since this has happened, I won't beat a dead horse and just post a quick reply: Catch-all solutions that say 'make any power up to your necessity' fits perfectly in rule zero fallacy. Also, I don't think that numina rules are so explicit, but implied inference from the previous revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T11:52:30-07:00","id":191581,"title":"","content":"Well, whatever the issue, unless you need a power that scales in dots, Numina are pretty good for whatever you need. Since Embeds don't scale in dots and we're given examples of Angels who have Embeds in power (not to mention it's said that the G-M created these subroutines <i>for </i>Angels, than I'd say it's a pretty fair fit to give them whatever Embeds you think are appropriate.<br /> <br /> Demon is very straightforward on the notion that the GM can alter things to suit the situation, such as by way of including resistance or contested checks on Embeds that don't seem to have them already. If you as a GM feel like an Embed such as Just Bruised is too powerful for the Angel to have, don't give it to them. I don't see the particular problem with this requiring the judgement of a GM. Hunter is much the same when it comes to designing monsters. Certain combinations of Dread Powers might be too much for your average hunter. Use your own judgement to determine that, and don't hesitate to not include one power or another if that's the case. It's pretty easy to work with that.<br /> <br /> I'm of the <i>personal </i>opinion that if I give them an Embed as a Numina, I'm probably going to introduce a single Essence cost or two. it's a decent limiter. I'd fluff it as given that Angels aren't physical beings like Demons, they need the extra material push of Essence to effect the same backdoors of reality. I'd also probably make them just use Power + Finesse, but if you felt like it you could treat it like other skill rolls for ephemeral beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-08-2014, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T14:20:37-07:00","id":191696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191509#post191509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this has happened, I won't beat a dead horse and just post a quick reply: Catch-all solutions that say 'make any power up to your necessity' fits perfectly in rule zero fallacy. Also, I don't think that numina rules are so explicit, but implied inference from the previous revision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't going to say anything because who the hell actually wants to argue about logical fallacies, but since you made a point to reiterate it, I want to contend that no, it's not a rule zero fallacy. I might come back when I've had a wink of sleep (so, tomorrow) and try to articulate <i>why</i> it isn't, unless some kind soul can break it down in the meantime. Until then, here's the full text of the rule zero fallacy so you can possibly puzzle it out on your own!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The </span></span></span><b>Oberoni Fallacy</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (also called the <i>Rule Zero</i></span></span></span><i><i> Fallacy</i></i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">) is the erroneous argument that the rules of a game aren't flawed because they can be ignored, or one or more &quot;house rules&quot; can be made as exceptions.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So, like I said, not rule 0 fallacy. You could argue that it's lazy design, or that the game leaves you hanging, but the fallacy is something different entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T15:32:20-07:00","id":191734,"title":"","content":"A lot of people equate &quot;create your own powers if those provided don't suit your needs&quot; to house ruling, and at that point it's easy to see how people could connect that to the Oberoni fallacy, especially because it's often short handed to &quot;it's not broken because I can houserule to fix it&quot;. However, the actual fallacy refers to ignoring or changing existing rules, not to creating new ones. A game system can never account for every possible situation, so the fact of the matter is you will always need to create rules to cover situations that the designers did not consider. You can call that house-ruling of you want to, but if you lump it under the rule 0 fallacy than you're calling every TTRPG &quot;broken&quot; because there will always be situations you need to &quot;house rule&quot; to &quot;fix&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T16:21:57-07:00","id":191779,"title":"","content":"My personal dissatisfaction with the angel power rules is that they are provided within a highly complex and tiered game system of influences and numinae and embeds and conditions and essence and what have you, which are then not elaborated with sufficient examples (this is subjective of course) and are brushed off with the ability to just create powers whenever however.<br /> <br /> If a game system is intended to be reliant on ST fiat and extensive improv then its best to be explicit about that and not to confuse the issue by providing such numerous and complicated rules that you are then encouraged to &quot;ignore&quot; for the lack of better term. One problem with having such a laissez faire attitude is that it keeps begging the question along the lines of &quot;so why bother having rule [blah] there in the first place?&quot; Some people are not very bothered by those questions but others are. It's a comprehension issue. I very much empathise with pcontop's position as I've spent a not insignificant amount of time trying to &quot;solve&quot; the write up of angel powers and figure out when, how and what to use. Mostly unsuccessfully so far. <br /> <br /> I understand *why* we have the write up that we have (compromises, space constraints, conventional wisdoms etc) but it certainly is not a chapter that is easy to use. I very much hope that the Storyteller's Guide provides more guidance on how to use angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T17:14:45-07:00","id":191840,"title":"","content":"Between the Numina given in the GMC Rules Update and all the Embeds Angels can potentially have, you've got a pretty vast grab bag of generic powers to flavor as you like. Honestly, they're the easiest part.<br /> <br /> Influences can be a bit impenetrable, but that's the most loosey goosey part of the whole thing. Using them in practice can help, and everything else is fairly straightforward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T19:23:05-07:00","id":191898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191779#post191779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand *why* we have the write up that we have (compromises, space constraints, conventional wisdoms etc) but it certainly is not a chapter that is easy to use. I very much hope that the Storyteller's Guide provides more guidance on how to use angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I found some parts of the section on ephemeral entities harder to follow than my textbooks on quantum physics and nuclear magnetic resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T00:38:43-07:00","id":192160,"title":"","content":"For me it wasn't particularly difficult to understand. Ephemeral Creatures come in 5 flavours of strong. They have three primary ways of interacting with the world. Influences allow them to subtly affect the world according to their focus. Manifestations allow them to show up and be spooky. Numina allow them to act overtly supernaturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T01:32:37-07:00","id":192187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191779#post191779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal dissatisfaction with the angel power rules is that they are provided within a highly complex and tiered game system of influences and numinae and embeds and conditions and essence and what have you, which are then not elaborated with sufficient examples (this is subjective of course) and are brushed off with the ability to just create powers whenever however. If a game system is intended to be reliant on ST fiat and extensive improv then its best to be explicit about that and not to confuse the issue by providing such numerous and complicated rules that you are then encouraged to &amp;quot;ignore&amp;quot; for the lack of better term. One problem with having such a laissez faire attitude is that it keeps begging the question along the lines of &amp;quot;so why bother having rule [blah] there in the first place?&amp;quot; Some people are not very bothered by those questions but others are. It's a comprehension issue. I very much empathise with pcontop's position as I've spent a not insignificant amount of time trying to &amp;quot;solve&amp;quot; the write up of angel powers and figure out when, how and what to use. Mostly unsuccessfully so far. I understand *why* we have the write up that we have (compromises, space constraints, conventional wisdoms etc) but it certainly is not a chapter that is easy to use. I very much hope that the Storyteller's Guide provides more guidance on how to use angels.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well there are basically four subsystems that make up the overall ephemeral entities system. Three of these systems (Influences, Manifestations, and Manifestation Conditions) are interconnected through the complex, tiered structure you mentioned. It's actually a lot less complicated than it looks once you grokk it, but it's written in a way that makes that very difficult to do, and indeed more examples would have gone a long way towards making it more approachable. The fourth subsystem (Numena) doesn't actually touch that web that the other three are tied up in. They're just pre-packaged abilities that ephemeral entities can use. These are the part of the system that Storytellers are encouraged to create their own. They do not replace the other three subsystems, so creating Numina does not necessitate, not even allow you to ignore the rest of the ephemeral entities system. It's just a way of giving angels, spirits, and ghosts a bag of tricks they can perform. Feel free to stick with the tricks provided, or to add your own, but the entities are still beholden to the rules of Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T14:22:13-07:00","id":192752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191159#post191159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not actually ephemeral beings and don't use their rules.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it's not a terribly important point.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do use mechanics that are applied to ephemeral beings like angels/spirits/ghosts( they didn't really in the wicked dead where they were discussed in fuller detail for baseline Requiem, but they do now as of Blood &amp;Smoke), with their own specific mechanics overlay ed upon them. Just wanted to point that out for everybody <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:01:50-07:00","id":194865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=183771#post183771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not need to hand wave anything. Demons try to escape in a car, the hunter angel has Finesse + Rank. Rank is used in place of any skill, save for where Attribute + Attribute is made instead (such as with perception). It specifically says that any task an angel needs to accomplish it can use Rank on, because that is part of its mission. If it tries to perform a task outside its mission, it cannot. (But angels are always on mission, if they're not, there is going to be a really big bang in a moment! and the demon's will have a new friend! ...or enemy?)<br /> <br /> Angels also have influences. All Ephemeral Entities have dots equal to their rank in Influences. An Angel's influences are things related to either (or both) it's nature or it's mission. Depending on how many dots it has in these influences, it is able to do more with them.<br /> <br /> In the above example, the demons are attempting to get away in a car. The angel is in pursuit. Slowing down the demon's by changing the traffic signs is within the scope of it's mission (It's a destroyer angel sent to chase and kill demons who will, of course, attempt escape). So, it rolls Finesse + Rank and you, as the storyteller simply decide whether success means all lights along the road go red, or a number of lights equal to rank or successes. Activating the sleepers in a nearby car? Power + Rank, each success awakens a mortal as a sleeper agent. (Not all mortals are sleeper agents, but one-shot NPC fodder don't need to be explained, Angels are adept at using whatever resources they happen to have in their local environment). Starting the car? Finesse + Rank, success turns the vehicle on. Finesse+Rank drives it.<br /> <br /> These are all solid rolls you as the story teller make and -could- fail on, either to represent an angel's momentary hesitation or confusion, or encountering a situation it does not know how to easily resolve quickly. This general performance in light of its mission affords angels some of the greatest power, and indeed gives them whatever tools they happen to need to perform their mission. Embeds and Exploits represent individual hacks the Demons have created in an effort to replicate this ability along with the more specific abilities of Numina.<br /> <br /> Or so is my understanding of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my understanding that Angels use Rank for Skills <i>directly</i> related to their mission - basically, the ones you would have given them dots in on their character sheet, if they were a mortal.<br /> <br /> They don't automatically <i>gain</i> Skills whenever they would be useful - although you could give them an Embed along those lines, I think. (Numina cost 4 or 5 new!XP IIRC, so compare that to Embeds if you're worried about how to adapt them.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, Angels don't have Influence: Stuff Related To My Mission. They have <i>specific</i> Influence(s) related to their mission.<br /> <br /> For example, your Destroyer Angel could have Influence: Electronics, perhaps, and that would let them unlock a door if they had enough dots in it ... but it could only do the lights thing if it had a lot of Influence dots, and it couldn't unlock a <i>wooden</i> door at all.<br /> <br /> Angels sooort of have access to all Embeds ... but in practice, that's just some fluff to make Demon more interesting. They are only actually <i>assigned</i> access to a few specific ones, represented by their inherent abilities - as described in God-Machine Chronicle.<br /> <br /> An Angel that starts Exploiting it's access to the God-Machine like that is probably a Demon in process of Falling. (Wow, that's a lot of capitalized terminology in one sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:27:01-07:00","id":194895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=194865#post194865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's my understanding that Angels use Rank for Skills <i>directly</i> related to their mission - basically, the ones you would have given them dots in on their character sheet, if they were a mortal.<br /> <br /> They don't automatically <i>gain</i> Skills whenever they would be useful - although you could give them an Embed along those lines, I think. (Numina cost 4 or 5 new!XP IIRC, so compare that to Embeds if you're worried about how to adapt them.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, Angels don't have Influence: Stuff Related To My Mission. They have <i>specific</i> Influence(s) related to their mission.<br /> <br /> For example, your Destroyer Angel could have Influence: Electronics, perhaps, and that would let them unlock a door if they had enough dots in it ... but it could only do the lights thing if it had a lot of Influence dots, and it couldn't unlock a <i>wooden</i> door at all.<br /> <br /> Angels sooort of have access to all Embeds ... but in practice, that's just some fluff to make Demon more interesting. They are only actually <i>assigned</i> access to a few specific ones, represented by their inherent abilities - as described in God-Machine Chronicle.<br /> <br /> An Angel that starts Exploiting it's access to the God-Machine like that is probably a Demon in process of Falling. (Wow, that's a lot of capitalized terminology in one sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they don't start with skills. They're an Ephemeral Being, they don't <i>get </i>skills. They can use Attribute + Rank to perform any task that they would require a skill to do if it relates to their mission. So, yes, if they had been a mortal, they'd have got skills in it. But instead, they use their Rank. Effectively giving them their Rank in <i>any </i>skills that they need to complete their mission. This seems a somewhat academic argument based entirely on my choice of wording.<br /> <br /> Angels <i>do </i>get &quot;Influence Stuff&quot; because much like a ghost has influence relating to their anchor, they have influence related to their mission. If they are anchored in creation because of say Sadness, then their anchor is sadness. So the ghost has Influence: Sadness. Similarly an angelic being is influencing the world of it's mission. So, if it's mission is to interact with electronics then yes, they'd be given Influence: Electronics. If their mission was to interact with people - such as protect them - then they'd have Influence: Human Beings. If their mission was &quot;doors&quot; then they'd have Influence: Doors.<br /> <br /> Influences are primarily utilised to relate with manifestations and manifestation conditions. If an angel needs to do something, such as start a car, it wouldn't call for an influence unless that was <i>directly </i>part of their mission. Instead they'd use either a skill check - like anyone else - or Numen. It's just that an angel, because they are Ephemeral, will always use Rank to make a skill check when it needs to. <i>Angels should never be performing tasks that do not directly relate to their mission. If they do, they are about to Fall.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T13:17:06-07:00","id":194933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=194895#post194895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they don't start with skills. They're an Ephemeral Being, they don't <i>get </i>skills. They can use Attribute + Rank to perform any task that they would require a skill to do if it relates to their mission. So, yes, if they had been a mortal, they'd have got skills in it. But instead, they use their Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Entities can use their Rank to represent their effective Skill rating in things <i>related to their concept</i>. A wolf-Spirit biting someone has effective dots in Brawl equal to Rank, because a wolf-Spirit would know how to bite someone.<br /> <br /> That same wolf-Spirit would not be able to add it's Rank to an attempt to dance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Effectively giving them their Rank in <i>any </i>skills that they need to complete their mission </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> If you're confused about why, the God-Machine doesn't predict and Angel's entire mission, it outfits it for a task, gives it orders, and sends it off. Thus, Angels are <i>not</i> assumed to possess whatever abilities they <i>end up</i> needing if it wasn't directly related to their original mission.<br /> <br /> They can't manifest arbitrary Numina, Influences, or Manifestations, and they can't duplicate arbitrary Skills or Merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Angels <i>do </i>get &quot;Influence Stuff&quot; because much like a ghost has influence relating to their anchor, they have influence related to their mission. If they are anchored in creation because of say Sadness, then their anchor is sadness. So the ghost has Influence: Sadness. Similarly an angelic being is influencing the world of it's mission. So, if it's mission is to interact with electronics then yes, they'd be given Influence: Electronics. If their mission was to interact with people - such as protect them - then they'd have Influence: Human Beings. If their mission was &quot;doors&quot; then they'd have Influence: Doors. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If a Guardian Angel had Influence: Humans to further it's mission, it would not then be able to Influence traffic lights, even if it would protect it's target to do so on that occasion. Angels don't have &quot;Influence: Mission&quot; written on their character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:19:14-07:00","id":195033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It specifically says that any task an angel needs to accomplish it can use Rank on, because that is part of its mission. If it tries to perform a task outside its mission, it cannot. (But angels are always on mission, if they're not, there is going to be a really big bang in a moment! and the demon's will have a new friend! ...or enemy?) </div> </div> </div>My original post on this thread. <i>They cannot act outside of their mission because they will Fall.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, that's what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Entities can use their Rank to represent their effective Skill rating in things <i>related to their concept</i>. A wolf-Spirit biting someone has effective dots in Brawl equal to Rank, because a wolf-Spirit would know how to bite someone.<br /> <br /> That same wolf-Spirit would not be able to add it's Rank to an attempt to dance. </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I said in my above quote. Unless the angel was supposed to use dance, why is he dancing? He is not. If he is dancing, he is about to Fall. He is an angel and must serve his purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No.<br /> <br /> If you're confused about why, the God-Machine doesn't predict and Angel's entire mission, it outfits it for a task, gives it orders, and sends it off. Thus, Angels are <i>not</i> assumed to possess whatever abilities they <i>end up</i> needing if it wasn't directly related to their original mission.<br /> <br /> They can't manifest arbitrary Numina, Influences, or Manifestations, and they can't duplicate arbitrary Skills or Merits. </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely correct. They cannot duplicate arbitrary skills and Numina they do not have. <i>They cannot have skills.</i><br /> So, basically, for your suggestion to be true you have to decide beforehand, while making the Angel, what skills qualify as on-mission. <i>Why not just give them skills if you're going to list what skills they do and do not have for their mission? </i>Never mind the fact that the idea behind embeds and exploits is that they are hacking subroutines that angels use as second nature. You know, like hot-wiring a car with a thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:43:21-07:00","id":195047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=195033#post195033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My original post on this thread. <i>They cannot act outside of their mission because they will Fall.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a <i>major</i> difference between &quot;directly related to their original mission&quot; and &quot;in the course of following their mission&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exactly what I said in my above quote. Unless the angel was supposed to use dance, why is he dancing? He is not. If he is dancing, he is about to Fall. He is an angel and must serve his purpose. </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A guardian Angel is assigned to guard John. Their mission is defined as &quot;prevent John from being injured or killed&quot;.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine equips them with the ability to assess possible threats and, if necessary, neutralize them.<br /> <br /> Despite their best efforts, John is kidnapped by, oh, let's say Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> The angel calculates that simply attacking the mansion where John is being held would result in him being killed, or his use as a hostage, (which would force the angel to abandon it's mission - inconceivable.)<br /> <br /> The angel now has to:</div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Find John inside the mansion (for which a mortal would use Investigation)</li> <li>Infiltrate the party being held there (for which a mortal would probably use Subterfuge and Socialize)</li> <li>Defeat any guards and escape with John (for which a mortal might use Firearms, Brawl, Weaponry etc.)</li> </ol>The Angel must perform <i>all three</i> tasks in the service of their original mission, but only the final one is <i>directly related</i> to their mission, and so they only possess Numen and other abilities related to it.<br /> <br /> As such, they may only apply their Rank as if it were a Skill rating to the final task, because that is the only task they innately understand.<br /> <br /> Do you see what I mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're absolutely correct. They cannot duplicate arbitrary skills and Numina they do not have. <i>They cannot have skills.</i> </div> </div> </div>You misread me. They cannot manifest Numina or Manifestations they were not equipped to manifest. Obviously, they may not have Skills at any time, but they may duplicate them in certain situations. And they may not <i>duplicate</i> Skills they were not equipped to duplicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, basically, for your suggestion to be true you have to decide beforehand, while making the Angel, what skills qualify as on-mission. <i>Why not just give them skills if you're going to list what skills they do and do not have for their mission?</i> </div> </div> </div>The same reason they use simplified Attributes, and why <i>all</i> mechanics related to Ephemeral Entities are simplified and generic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Never mind the fact that the idea behind embeds and exploits is that they are hacking subroutines that angels use as second nature. You know, like hot-wiring a car with a thought? </div> </div> </div>You can decide they represent that in your games, but in the basic rules, Angels <i>can't</i> manifest arbitrary Numina, Manifestations, or Influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:54:30-07:00","id":195079,"title":"","content":"I fear we are having a communication error as I both of us appear unable to communicate our points.<br /> <br /> I <i>did not</i> claim that Angels could manifest arbitrary <i>Numina, Manifestations or Influences. </i><b>None of these things are </b><i>Skills </i>and as a result have nothing to do with any of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The God-Machine Chronicle, p.220</b><br /> Ephemeral beings don\u2019t possess skills, but don\u2019t suffer unskilled penalties as long as the action they\u2019re attempting is appropriate to their former self, nature, or mission. They roll the appropriate Attribute + Rank for actions relating directly to their concept, or Attribute + Attribute for actions like surprise and perception. </div> </div> </div>This isn't very ambiguous. If an Ephemeral Being is attempting to perform a task you, the Storyteller, ask yourself: <i>Is this directly related to their concept?</i> In the case of an Angel this means<i> it's self, nature or mission. </i>Generally <i>mission </i>is what's important to an angel. If, such as in my prior examples, it is say <i>starting a car to chase a target it has been tasked with the retrieval or destruction of </i>and so the Angel here rolls Attribute + Rank because <i>it does not possess the drive skill and does not suffer unskilled penalties because it is performing an action appropriate to it's <b>self, nature or mission. </b></i><br /> <br /> None of that has <i>anything</i> to do with <b>Influences, Manifestations or Numina.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 07-11-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:05:09-07:00","id":195091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=195079#post195079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear we are having a communication error as I both of us appear unable to communicate our points.<br /> <br /> <b>I did not claim that Angels could manifest arbitrary Numina, Manifestations or Influences.</b> None of these things are Skills and as a result have nothing to do with any of that.<br /> <br /> This isn't very ambiguous. If an Ephemeral Being is attempting to perform a task you, the Storyteller, ask yourself: Is this directly related to their concept? In the case of an Angel this means it's self, nature or mission. Generally mission is what's important to an angel. If, such as in my prior examples, it is say starting a car to chase a target it has been tasked with the retrieval or destruction of and so the Angel here rolls Attribute + Rank because it does not possess the drive skill and does not suffer unskilled penalties because it is performing an action appropriate to it's self, nature or mission.<br /> <br /> None of that has anything to do with Influences, Manifestations or Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>You stated that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Never mind the fact that the idea behind embeds and exploits is that they are hacking subroutines that angels use as second nature. You know, like hot-wiring a car with a thought?</i> </div> </div> </div>They can't use Embeds and Exploits like that. They can use <i>specific</i> Embeds they were assigned access to by the God-Machine, as represented by their Numina, Manifestations, and Influences.<br /> <br /> And if you think <i>any action an entity could conceivably take</i> is somehow therefore &quot;<i>relating directly to their concept&quot;</i>, well ... that's strange. But even if that made sense, why does it not apply to Ghosts or Spirits (such as our dancing wolf-Spirit,) then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:16:04-07:00","id":195093,"title":"","content":"Embeds are abilities demons possess to mimic the abilities they once possessed as angels. The purpose of the statement was to illustrate that an embed does not need to be converted into numina, as many of the abilities an embed gives you - such as download knowledge - are replicated by the effect of an Ephemeral Being being able to use any skill without penalty in the pursuit of his mission. How does he achieve this? From a story point, he's probably downloading that knowledge from the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> As I stated in my posts prior I gave examples of how, using only the Ephemeral Creatures rules, one could replicate the abilities (or even better them) of many embeds that Demon characters can acquire. Therefore, the statement, an angel can &quot;use embeds without a second thought&quot; is illustrating their far greater abilities within both rules and lore.<br /> <br /> <b>No. I think: </b><i>An <b>Angel</b> can take any conceivable action that it must in order to complete its mission.</i> Just as a ghost can take any action conceivable to it's <b>self </b>and a spirit can take any action conceivable to it's <b>nature.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:20:20-07:00","id":195095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>No. I think: </b><i>An <b>Angel</b> can take any conceivable action that it must in order to complete its mission.</i> Just as a ghost can take any action conceivable to it's <b>self </b>and a spirit can take any action conceivable to it's <b>nature.</b> </div> </div> </div>But they only treat Rank as Skill dots if it <i>relates directly</i> to their mission/self/nature.<br /> <br /> All actions they take are possible <i>within</i> their concept, but not all <i>relate directly</i> to their concept. If they did - which would severely limit the actions they can take - why make a distinction in the first place?<br /> <br /> If you want an Angel to be able to have access to Download Knowledge, you can give it that as a Numen.* But it is no more an inherent ability of all Angels than it is of any other Ephemeral Entity.<br /> <br /> *(Heck, houserule it so they all have that ability, if you want.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-11-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:31:03-07:00","id":195101,"title":"","content":"Your Dancing Wolf spirit would lose it's immunity from unskilled penalties and have to roll Attribute only, not Attribute + Rank. Why? Because it is not a spirit of dance. An Angel's powers are more broad, why? Because it is not based on a concept, it is based on a task. Which means any intermediary task that it must perform to complete it's mission, it can use this ability on.<br /> <br /> A Ghost must define itself by whom it was: the <b>self</b>. This is going to be narrow, it can't gain this immunity to unskilled penalties on anything it couldn't do as a living person because doing so would violate it's <b>self</b>.<br /> <br /> A Spirit must define itself by it's <b>nature</b>, such as wolf. This is going to be narrow, but not as narrow as a ghost. It can gain it's immunity from unskilled penalties on anything it could do with wolves, but nothing else.<br /> <br /> An Angel must define itself by it's <b>mission</b>, such as &quot;Capture or Kill detected Demon.&quot; This is less narrow than the above with the spirit. It can gain it's immunity from unskilled penalties on anything it could do that help it capture or kill a detected demon. (Such as steal a car in order to pursue said detected demon.)<br /> <br /> You seem to think I am saying that, mechanically, they are able to just use an embed? No. They don't need to use mechanical embeds. These are cheats demons made to do the things angels can do. Can an angel replicate anything an embed can do? Yes. Why? Because it is connected to the God-Machine. It can't just do whatever it wants because it has a mission and if it goes off mission it loses all it's bonuses. Not to mention it is probably falling.<br /> <br /> Some embeds are better than others and do things that cannot easily be handled with the angel simply being able to unlock a door it needs to to perform it's mission - such as Just Bruised. In these cases, you don't use a skill, you probably use either an identical Numen or an Influence (such as Strengthen).<br /> <br /> But, if an angel needs to unlock a door to complete it's mission, this <i>directly relates</i> to it's mission as it <i>cannot</i> complete it's mission if it <i>cannot get past this door.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T09:51:23-07:00","id":195576,"title":"","content":"That isn't what the word &quot;directly&quot; means. Some thing can be directly <i>or indirectly</i> related to something, or completely unrelated.<br /> <br /> A Ghost's concept is based on it's former self; a Spirit's concept is based on it's nature, and an Angel's concept is based on the mission they were assigned.<br /> <br /> <i>All</i> of these have some actions that are directly related to that concept (which receive a bonus based on Rank), some actions that are antithetical to their concept (which would be inconceivable to them), and some actions which are <i>neither</i> directly related nor antithetical to their concept, like a combat-focused being that finds itself needing to dance.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in the text to suggest that this mechanic behaves differently for different types of Ephemeral Entity. Quite the opposite, in fact.<br /> <br /> You've argued that the existence of an Embed that allows Demons to download Skills justifies this interpretation, but that would make it the <i>only</i> Embed that all Angels have access to. Why? It's not exactly something that would make thematic or logical sense, and nowhere is it suggested that all Angels had access to this Embed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 07-12-2014, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T11:16:16-07:00","id":195619,"title":"","content":"So, an angel whose mission it was to kill a specific person would be programmed by the God-Machine with certain tools that would help it in that task (Embeds), represented mechanically by being Able to roll Attribute + Rank. Let's say that in order to kill the target, the angel finds that the best method would be to infiltrate his dance studio and leave a bomb in his dressing room. Planting a bomb is a skill the angel would likely be programmed with, as it is directly relevant to the mission. Disguising itself is another ability likely to be needed on an assassination mission. However, if the angel needs to audition to join the target's dance troupe, dancing is not really directly related to assassination. Now, if infiltrating a dance studio was a planned part of the mission to begin with, dancing talent would probably be another high priority on the list of embeds to include. If, on the other hand, the original plan had been to kill the target in some other way, and the whole dance thing was an unexpected turn if events, dancing is unlikely to have been included in the angel's programming unless the God Machine expected it to be needed to complete the mission. So even though in the moment dancing might be helping the angel complete its mission, it may not be directly related, and therefore would not be eligible for an Attribute + Rank roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T11:34:11-07:00","id":195626,"title":"","content":"As another example, use the original Matrix film. In this analogy, the crew of the Nebuchadnezzar are angels and their Operator is the God-Machine. (I know Angels are more commonly compared to Agents, but just bear with me.) The training programs that Tank can download straight into their brains are basically Embeds. When they went to take Neo to see the Oracle, they expected to need all of that combat training, parkour, knowledge about Agents, etc. because it's always a dangerous proposition to jack into the Matrix, which is an essential part of the mission given that's where the Oracle lives. However, they expected to just be visiting her apartment, so they didn't think to give anyone an Embedvfor flying helicopters. Therefore, when the shit hit the fan and Neo found himself unexpectedly needing to ask Trinity &quot;can you fly that&quot;, she had to respond &quot;not yet&quot; because she hadn't been programmed with that particular Embed for that particular mission. At this point the analogy breaks down, because Trinity was able to stream the training program while still jacked in, while for angels that is, as far as we know, not an option for Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T12:03:38-07:00","id":195646,"title":"","content":"I'd take a more impressionistic approach to judging the difference between on and off mission. Is the skill/act something that an undercover spy would reasonably be able to improvise because they're a badass secret agent? Or is it out of context? Hotwiring a car to chase after your objective, even if carjacking wasn't an anticipated need, seems in-genre. Abruptly being a master painter or dancer is much more of a stretch - though Numina to compensate don't seem out of bounds.<br /> <br /> I dont think anyone's arguing that angels can just use anything that's an embed, but embeds represent use of angelic capabilities, and the two kinds of characters are run on different systems. Some parts of what a demon treats as Download Knowledge can be represented just with the way ephemeral beings use attribute+rank. Some parts are better represented as numina. Figuring out the exact translation algorithm is utterly tangential to actually playing or running the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:30:07-07:00","id":195898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=195619#post195619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, an angel whose mission it was to kill a specific person would be programmed by the God-Machine with certain tools that would help it in that task (Embeds), represented mechanically by being Able to roll Attribute + Rank. Let's say that in order to kill the target, the angel finds that the best method would be to infiltrate his dance studio and leave a bomb in his dressing room. Planting a bomb is a skill the angel would likely be programmed with, as it is directly relevant to the mission. Disguising itself is another ability likely to be needed on an assassination mission. However, if the angel needs to audition to join the target's dance troupe, dancing is not really directly related to assassination. Now, if infiltrating a dance studio was a planned part of the mission to begin with, dancing talent would probably be another high priority on the list of embeds to include. If, on the other hand, the original plan had been to kill the target in some other way, and the whole dance thing was an unexpected turn if events, dancing is unlikely to have been included in the angel's programming unless the God Machine expected it to be needed to complete the mission. So even though in the moment dancing might be helping the angel complete its mission, it may not be directly related, and therefore would not be eligible for an Attribute + Rank roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely what I was saying, yes. Thank you!<br /> <br /> I was simply adding that if he decides to go dancing, he's either getting to close to or actually falling and that's a whole other can of worms.<br /> <br /> Remember: An angel can fall for the simple act of hesitation and confusion at being confronted with somewhere where it has to think for itself. It does not always fall simply because of pure and direct <i>disobedience</i>. It falls because it makes an inherent act of free will: <b>a decision.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 07-12-2014, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T20:39:09-07:00","id":195968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=195626#post195626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another example, use the original Matrix film. In this analogy, the crew of the Nebuchadnezzar are angels and their Operator is the God-Machine. (I know Angels are more commonly compared to Agents, but just bear with me.) The training programs that Tank can download straight into their brains are basically Embeds. When they went to take Neo to see the Oracle, they expected to need all of that combat training, parkour, knowledge about Agents, etc. because it's always a dangerous proposition to jack into the Matrix, which is an essential part of the mission given that's where the Oracle lives. However, they expected to just be visiting her apartment, so they didn't think to give anyone an Embedvfor flying helicopters. Therefore, when the shit hit the fan and Neo found himself unexpectedly needing to ask Trinity &quot;can you fly that&quot;, she had to respond &quot;not yet&quot; because she hadn't been programmed with that particular Embed for that particular mission. At this point the analogy breaks down, because Trinity was able to stream the training program while still jacked in, while for angels that is, as far as we know, not an option for Angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reprogramming an angel's Numina - and even reconfiguring it's physical form - seems like something that you could do at certain Infrastructure; it probably takes time and resources (otherwise the G-M wouldn't use tailored angels for missions but instead reprogram flexible angels) but it makes sense to me that there's sort of an angelic bodyshop. It might even be the same type of Infrastructure where retired angels are taken for dismantling and recycling.<br /> <br /> The other similar concept I'd probably run with is the idea that angels can touch the quasi-omniscience of the G-M to try to gain knowledge related to their mission. I think you could model it as the ability to do research extended actions at a much faster rate than normal without needing a library, etc. Essentially they enter communion with the God-Machine and hope to find what they need in the sea of information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T09:00:37-07:00","id":203000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=191696#post191696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't going to say anything because who the hell actually wants to argue about logical fallacies, but since you made a point to reiterate it, I want to contend that no, it's not a rule zero fallacy. I might come back when I've had a wink of sleep (so, tomorrow) and try to articulate <i>why</i> it isn't, unless some kind soul can break it down in the meantime. Until then, here's the full text of the rule zero fallacy so you can possibly puzzle it out on your own!<br /> <br /> So, like I said, not rule 0 fallacy. You could argue that it's lazy design, or that the game leaves you hanging, but the fallacy is something different entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way I see it,the numina as listed have a given power level consistently. So if you are saying 'place any power you desire as a numina to make angels as powerful as they are supposed to be', is a rule zero fallacy. Numina as 'anything goes' is a houserule, in GMC. To make a parallel, I could make a vampiric discipline that has double effectiveness of vigor for the same costs, given that new disciplines can be created, but that'd be way outside design space!<br /> <br /> On another subject, embeds have been designed and balanced for the fragile things demons are in their covers. As such, they would make angels quite simply overpowered, given their unnatainable dicepools and immaterial nature. Numina and influences, as listed in the books from GMC and on, are not a very good replacement for 'all embeds from angel type'. The huge dicepools can be something like that, but only in an abstract, stopgap uncrunchy way. We need something else for running angels.<br /> <br /> I would very much like a book with more developed rules for angels, as the line develops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T02:19:12-07:00","id":208043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=203000#post203000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The way I see it,the numina as listed have a given power level consistently. So if you are saying 'place any power you desire as a numina to make angels as powerful as they are supposed to be', is a rule zero fallacy. Numina as 'anything goes' is a houserule, in GMC. To make a parallel, I could make a vampiric discipline that has double effectiveness of vigor for the same costs, given that new disciplines can be created, but that'd be way outside design space!.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why would the GMC talk about ephemeral beings having the supernatural powers of other beings in their numina list when there are no other supernatural beings other than ephemerals in the God-Machine Chronicle book? If the GMC said ephemerals couldn't have the powers of other supernaturals then you'd have a point, but a book not mentioning something one way or the other is not retconning something out.<br /> <br /> Demon specifically talks about angels having embeds, but not having exploits, well I don't know about you but I don't need an engraved invitation written on stone from Mt Sinai on a silver platter that they actually mean that angels can have embeds, I figure I'll take them at their word.<br /> <br /> Nor does the GMC book coming out retcon vampire ghosts from Mythologies, The Beast as a spirit from Blood Sorcery, or the Blind Mother from Night Horrors who all have disciplines as numina, or that in werewolf books spirits can have gifts because gifts come from the spirits in the first place so why can't they have them? In mage books spirits can have rotes as numina and ghost mages definitely do, or Geists having manifestations as numina in Geist. So Demon is the fifth gameline that has ephemerals with expanded numina lists, that's not actually news at this point. <br /> <br /> Correction, sixth gameline, because the Principle's fiery angels can also include transmutations as numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 07-25-2014, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T09:45:33-07:00","id":208417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/183320-angels-how-powerful?p=203000#post203000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it,the numina as listed have a given power level consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at Blast.<br /> <br /> Now look at Aggressive Meme.<br /> <br /> If you think these things are equivalent in scale, then absolutely nothing will make the concept of transplanting other powers to Numina make sense to you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Moderator edit (Darksider). Satchel, please stay out of this thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-26-2014, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}